                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_34\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit (fix_commit_diff.txt) modifies `setHalfwayBuffer` in\nsrc/jpcsp/HLE/modules/sceAtrac3plus.java, replacing:\n\n    int maxSizeBeforeFirstWrap = bufferSize - ((bufferSize - info.inputFileDataOffset) % info.atracBytesPerFrame);\n    int maxSizeAfterFirstWrap = bufferSize - (bufferSize % info.atracBytesPerFrame);\n    inputBuffer = new pspFileBuffer(addr, maxSizeBeforeFirstWrap, maxSizeAfterFirstWrap, readSize, readSize);\n\nwith a version that only performs this alignment when `readSize < bufferSize`\n(i.e. only when the buffer is not already full), otherwise it just uses the\nraw `bufferSize` for both values. The bug was that the alignment computation\nwas applied unconditionally, even when the buffer was already fully read\n(readSize == bufferSize), causing an incorrect (too small) maxSize to be used\nfor a fully-populated buffer, leading to wrong wrap-around behavior in\nsceAtracGetStreamDataInfo/related streaming logic.\n\ncandidate_34's diff introduces exactly these three lines verbatim as a new\naddition:\n  - It changes `inputBuffer = new pspFileBuffer(addr, bufferSize, readSize, readSize);`\n    (previously present, with no alignment logic at all) to\n    the unconditional alignment computation identical to what the fix commit\n    later guards with the `if (readSize < bufferSize)` check.\n  - It also adds the corresponding `maxSizeBeforeFirstWrap`/`maxSizeAfterFirstWrap`\n    fields and the new pspFileBuffer constructor overload in pspFileBuffer.java\n    to support the (now buggy) two-value buffer sizing scheme.\n\nEarlier candidates (e.g. candidate_16, which introduced setHalfwayBuffer)\nonly had the simple, non-aligned `new pspFileBuffer(addr, bufferSize, readSize, readSize)`\ncall, which did not exhibit the bug. candidate_25 only added debug logging\nunrelated to this logic. candidate_34 is therefore the first commit to\nintroduce the exact unconditional alignment logic that the fix commit\ncorrects, making it the bug-introducing commit.\n"
                }
              }
